    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "88f1cd5d_62de7882",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1947461
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-30T09:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Inet4Address and Inet6Address is a subclass of InetAddress.\nI don\u0027t think we have a single standard way to convert the v4 address to the v6 address.\nOne way is v4-mapped v6 address but another way is putting the v4 address to the first 4 bytes of the 16 bytes v6 address.\n\nSo If we want Struct to handle conversion from v4 address to v6 address, we need a new Struct Type to tell Struct about how to convert.\nAlso, it\u0027s not clear how to convert byteBuffer to Struct.\nIf we put the v4 address to the first 4 bytes of 16 bytes, we can not distinguish if this was a v4 address or v6 address.\nMaybe it\u0027s fine to assume the address was v4 address if last 12 bytes are zero but I\u0027m not sure.\n\nFor this CL, I feel it\u0027s simpler to do this on the caller side.",
      "parentUuid": "7042d81e_3720c64a",
      "revId": "42d37bad8d69e53e166384eb6573efc48bd55aca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e63f68bd_02a2e5cd",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-31T21:11:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There\u0027s only 3 valid ways to do it:\n\n4 bytes, then 12 zeroes \u003c-- but this confuses lots of stuff, so requires a separate flag to clarify whether you mean v4 or v6\n\n12 zeroes, then 4 bytes \u003c-- but this confuses ::1 vs 0.0.0.1, so requires a seperate flag to clarify whether you mean v4 or v6\n\nas such the only \u0027reliable and sane\u0027 way to do it is via ::ffff:1.2.3.4 encoding.\n\nWe should just allow Struct to take \u0027InetAddress\u0027 instead of Inet6Address either for the IPV6 annotation, or for a new IP annotation.\n\nIndeed I\u0027m pretty sure we already have code somewhere in the stack that uses IPv6 struct field to store IPv4.\n\nIndeed doesn\u0027t take long to find toIpv4MappedAddressBytes and discover there\u0027s ample room for improvement.",
      "parentUuid": "88f1cd5d_62de7882",
      "revId": "42d37bad8d69e53e166384eb6573efc48bd55aca",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
